      "description": "Watch Sevilla vs Valencia highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 11, 2026. On September 11, 2026, Sevilla and Valencia faced off in a high-stakes La Liga encounter where tactical discipline and defensive resilience dominated the narrative for much of the evening. Both sides struggled to break the deadlock in a match defined by narrow margins and a dramatic late intervention. VAR Drama and Midfield Stalemate The contest began with a significant moment of tension in the 10th minute when the referee halted play for a VAR check regarding a potential penalty for Sevilla . After a brief period of uncertainty, the decision was made not to award the spot-kick, much to the relief of the Valencia faithful. The first half continued as a physical battle, highlighted by a yellow card for Ryunosuke Sato following a rough challenge. Despite several corner opportunities for both teams, neither side could find the clinical edge required to open the scoring before the interval. The Breakthrough and Tactical Shifts As the second half progressed, both managers turned to their benches to find a spark. Sevilla introduced fresh energy with Robbie Ure and Chidera Ejuke , while Valencia brought on Pablo Maffeo to shore up the flanks. The game’s defining moment arrived in the 81st minute. Giorgi Kochorashvili , who had entered the fray as a substitute, delivered a pinpoint cross that found Juan Iglesias . The Sevilla man made no mistake, powering a header into the back of the net to ignite the home crowd. Valencia's Late Push Denied Trailing by a goal, Valencia committed men forward in the final stages, controlling 54% of the overall possession. Arnaut Danjuma attempted to rescue a point with a strike from distance in the 90th minute, but his effort failed to test the goalkeeper. Deep into stoppage time, the Sevilla defense stood firm, with Andres Castrin and Kike Salas making vital clearances to weather the storm. When the final whistle blew after nine minutes of added time, Sevilla emerged victorious, having successfully navigated a tense battle to secure all three points."
