      "description": "Watch Valencia vs Barcelona highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 6, 2026. On September 6, 2026 , the spotlight of La Liga fell on a classic encounter between Valencia and Barcelona . The match promised a high-octane battle as both teams sought to establish their dominance in the league standings, creating an atmosphere of intense anticipation among the fans. Barcelona’s Early Surge and VAR Drama Barcelona wasted no time in asserting their authority, controlling the tempo from the opening whistle. The breakthrough came as early as the 6th minute when Lamine Yamal produced a moment of magic, lofting an exquisite lob over the goalkeeper following an assist from Fermín López . The visitors thought they had doubled their lead shortly after through Yamal again, but a VAR review intervened to rule the goal out for offside. Despite the disallowed goal, the pressure remained relentless. In the 22nd minute, Anthony Gordon turned provider for Fermín López , who clinicaly finished with his left foot to give Barcelona a comfortable cushion. Valencia struggled to find their rhythm, hindered by tactical fouls and a yellow card for Pau Cubarsí as they tried to halt the Catalan momentum before the break. Tactical Shifts and Second-Half Dominance The second half mirrored the first, with Barcelona displaying slick passing and movement. In the 50th minute, a wonderful team goal saw Raphinha tap the ball home at the far post after a selfless pass from Fermín López . As the match progressed, substitutions played a key role. The introduction of Dani Olmo in the 75th minute added fresh creative impetus to the midfield. Olmo made an immediate impact, providing the assist for Pedri to score in the 79th minute with a well-placed right-footed shot. Valencia 's frustrations grew as Arnau Martínez received a yellow card for a heavy challenge. The scoring was rounded off in the 84th minute when Lamine Yamal secured his second of the night. After another VAR check for a potential infringement, the goal was confirmed, cementing a dominant display by the visitors. Closing Stages and Statistical Superiority As the clock ticked down, Barcelona remained in complete control, finishing the match with an impressive 73% ball possession. Dani Olmo nearly added a sixth in the dying minutes, but his effort missed the target. Valencia attempted late surges through Hugo Duro and Harvey Elliott , but the defensive solidity of Barcelona ensured a clean sheet. The final whistle confirmed a masterclass performance, leaving the home side to reflect on a challenging night at the office."
